{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.ComplexDilogarithmInversion","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.ComplexDilogarithmInversion","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.ComplexDilogarithmOnCut","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.LiTwoNegOne","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Convex.PathConnected","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Complex.Convex"],"declarations":22,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.continuousAt_re_cLiTwoExt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.continuousAt_re_cLiTwoExt","kind":"theorem","line":386,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithmInversion.lean#L386-L422","doc":"**`Re Li₂` is continuous at every point of the cut `(1,∞)`.**\n\nTwo-sided, which is what the transport needs: at `φ = π` the argument `x·y`\nreaches the cut point from below and `y/x` reaches the *same* point from above\n(Route 37 G8), so a one-sided statement would have to be proved twice.\n\n`cLiTwoExt` itself is **not** continuous there — it jumps by `2πi·log x` — so\nthe `.re` is load-bearing rather than cosmetic. `envelopeS` takes `.re` of every\nterm, which is exactly what makes the endpoint reachable. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.continuousAt_re_log_neg_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.continuousAt_re_log_neg_sq","kind":"theorem","line":370,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithmInversion.lean#L370-L382","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.re_log_neg_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.re_log_neg_sq","kind":"theorem","line":337,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithmInversion.lean#L337-L368","doc":"**The rewrite that carries the theorem.** `arg (−w)` jumps by `2π` across\nthe positive reals; `|arg w|` does not jump there at all, and\n\n    Re(log(−w)²) = (log‖w‖)² − (|arg w| − π)²\n\nholds for **every** `w ≠ 0`, including on both jump loci. Route 37 G6 checks it\n*on* the positive and negative reals, not merely near them. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.re_invCombo_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.re_invCombo_eq","kind":"theorem","line":318,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithmInversion.lean#L318-L333","doc":"**`Re (invCombo w) = −π²/6` on an open neighbourhood of the cut.**\n\nThe two clauses tile a full neighbourhood of any real `x > 1`: nearby points are\neither off the real axis — where `invCombo_eq` applies — or real with real part\nabove `1`, where `re_invCombo_ofReal` does. That is what makes the continuity\nbelow **two-sided** rather than one-sided; Route 37 G8 measures that the\ntransport needs both sides, `x·y` reaching `w₀` from below and `y/x` from above. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.re_invCombo_ofReal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.re_invCombo_ofReal","kind":"theorem","line":299,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithmInversion.lean#L299-L316","doc":"**`Re (invCombo x) = −π²/6` for real `x ≥ 1`** — i.e. *on the cut*, where\n`invCombo_eq` does not reach.\n\nThis is `re_inversion_identity` rearranged, and it is the reason only the real\npart is claimed here: the imaginary part of `cLiTwoExt` on the cut is\n`−π·log x`, which the tree does not prove. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.re_div_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.re_div_two","kind":"theorem","line":296,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithmInversion.lean#L296-L297","doc":"`(z / 2).re = z.re / 2`. Stated once rather than re-`simp`ed at each use. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.log_neg_ofReal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.log_neg_ofReal","kind":"theorem","line":287,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithmInversion.lean#L287-L294","doc":"`Complex.log` of a negative real, in the form the real part needs. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.invCombo_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.invCombo_eq","kind":"theorem","line":260,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithmInversion.lean#L260-L283","doc":"**The inversion identity, as a full complex equation on `ℂ ∖ [0,∞)`.**\n\nRoute 37 G2 checks it at 16 points — both half planes, the negative reals, both\nsides of the cut, near the branch point, and far out — all chosen *off* the 5₂\narc configuration, so nothing peculiar to that locus can be carrying it.\n\nThe base point is `−1`, where both dilogarithm terms are `cLiTwoExt (−1) =\n−π²/12` (`cLiTwoExt_neg_one`) and `log 1 = 0` kills the third. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.hasDerivAt_invCombo","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.hasDerivAt_invCombo","kind":"theorem","line":230,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithmInversion.lean#L230-L258","doc":"**The derivative of the inversion combination vanishes on `ℂ ∖ [0,∞)`.**\n\nThree derivatives, each already in the tree or in Mathlib, whose sum is\n`(−log(1−w) + log(1−1/w) + log(−w))/w`. The bracket vanishes by\n`log_one_sub_inv_add_log_neg`, and that is the entire content. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.invCombo","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.invCombo","kind":"def","line":226,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithmInversion.lean#L226-L228","doc":"`invCombo w = Li₂(w) + Li₂(1/w) + ½·log(−w)²`. Constant on `ℂ ∖ [0,∞)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.log_one_sub_inv_add_log_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.log_one_sub_inv_add_log_neg","kind":"theorem","line":177,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithmInversion.lean#L177-L222","doc":"**The additive law for the two logarithms in the inversion derivative.**\n\n`(1 − 1/w)·(−w) = 1 − w` is algebra; that the *principal* logarithms add is not.\nIt needs `arg (1 − 1/w) + arg (−w) ∈ (−π, π]`, and the two arguments have\nstrictly **opposite** signs throughout `ℂ ∖ [0,∞)` — `Im (1 − 1/w) = Im w/‖w‖²`\nagainst `Im (−w) = −Im w` — so the sum is trapped between them.\n\n⚠ The hypothesis is load-bearing. On `(0,1)` both arguments are `+π` and the sum\nis `2π`: Route 37 G5 checks that the law **fails** there, so dropping `invDomain`\ngives a false lemma rather than a harder one. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.arg_nonpos_of_mem_slitPlane","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.arg_nonpos_of_mem_slitPlane","kind":"theorem","line":166,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithmInversion.lean#L166-L175","doc":"On the slit plane, `arg ≤ 0` is equivalent to `Im ≤ 0` — the `Im = 0` case\nbeing carried by `Re > 0`. **Off** the slit plane it is false (`arg = π` at a\nnegative real, whose imaginary part is `0`), which is exactly why `invDomain`\ncannot be widened. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.one_sub_inv_mem_slitPlane","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.one_sub_inv_mem_slitPlane","kind":"theorem","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithmInversion.lean#L138-L162","doc":"`1 − 1/w` never lands on `log`'s cut when `w` avoids `[0,∞)`. Needed twice:\nto know `log (1 − 1/w)` is not the junk value, and — through\n`arg_nonpos_of_mem_slitPlane` — to bound its argument. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.inv_mem_invDomain","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.inv_mem_invDomain","kind":"theorem","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithmInversion.lean#L128-L136","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.mem_notCut_of_mem_invDomain","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.mem_notCut_of_mem_invDomain","kind":"theorem","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithmInversion.lean#L123-L126","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.ne_zero_of_mem_invDomain","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.ne_zero_of_mem_invDomain","kind":"theorem","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithmInversion.lean#L119-L121","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.isPreconnected_invDomain","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.isPreconnected_invDomain","kind":"theorem","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithmInversion.lean#L110-L117","doc":"**`ℂ ∖ [0,∞)` is connected.** It is star-shaped about `−1`, being the image\nof the slit plane — star-shaped about `1` — under negation. This is what lets\nthe constant be pinned at an *interior* point; on a half plane the only base\npoint where `invCombo` is computable sits on the boundary, and the constant\nwould have to be recovered by a limit. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.neg_one_mem_invDomain","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.neg_one_mem_invDomain","kind":"theorem","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithmInversion.lean#L106-L108","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.isOpen_invDomain","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.isOpen_invDomain","kind":"theorem","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithmInversion.lean#L103-L104","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.neg_mem_slitPlane_of_mem_invDomain","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.neg_mem_slitPlane_of_mem_invDomain","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithmInversion.lean#L100-L101","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.mem_invDomain_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.mem_invDomain_iff","kind":"theorem","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithmInversion.lean#L96-L98","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.invDomain","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.invDomain","kind":"def","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexDilogarithmInversion.lean#L90-L94","doc":"**`ℂ ∖ [0,∞)`**, the domain of the inversion formula: the slit plane\nreflected through the origin. Taking it as `-slitPlane` rather than as a raw\n`setOf` is what makes `starConvex_one_slitPlane.neg` apply, and connectedness is\nthe only nontrivial thing needed of it. ","signatureChunk":0}]}